window.MOCK_BANK=(window.MOCK_BANK||[]).concat([{"id":"contrast-001","criterion":"1.1","lo":1,"tag":"Utility and warranty","prompt":"A reporting service meets its agreed availability target but cannot produce the forecast its customer requires. Which assessment is supported?","options":["Warranty is supported, but the required utility is missing","Utility is supported, but the required warranty is missing","Both utility and warranty are demonstrated by availability","Neither utility nor warranty can be assessed from these facts"],"why":"Availability supports warranty; the missing required function concerns utility. Meeting one does not establish the other.","whyNl":"De afgesproken beschikbaarheid wordt gehaald: dat ondersteunt warranty. De vereiste forecastfunctie ontbreekt: utility ontbreekt voor die behoefte. Niet alles is dus onvoldoende, maar beschikbaarheid bewijst ook niet dat de dienst de juiste functie heeft.","hook":"Separate required functionality from agreed conditions of use.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-002","criterion":"1.1","lo":1,"tag":"Utility and warranty","prompt":"A service can perform the required calculations. It also maintains agreed response times under the expected load. Which pairing is correct?","options":["Required calculation: utility; assured performance under load: warranty","Required calculation: warranty; assured performance under load: utility","Required calculation: output; assured performance under load: outcome","Required calculation: outcome; assured performance under load: output"],"why":"The capability addresses the need; assurance about capacity and performance supports use. Outputs and outcomes concern deliverables and resulting effects, not this distinction.","whyNl":"De berekenmogelijkheid is functionaliteit, dus utility. Afgesproken prestaties onder belasting gaan over bruikbaarheid en capaciteit, dus warranty. Een gegenereerd rapport zou output zijn; een betere beslissing dankzij het rapport een outcome.","hook":"Can do the task; can be relied on under agreed conditions.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-003","criterion":"1.1","lo":1,"tag":"Consumer roles","prompt":"A manager defines the service requirements, approves its budget and uses it. Which conclusion is correct?","options":["The manager performs customer, sponsor and user roles","The manager is a sponsor, so cannot also be a customer","The manager is a customer, while the provider performs the user role","The manager performs one consumer role determined by seniority"],"why":"Roles describe responsibilities and actions; one person can perform several. Seniority does not make the roles mutually exclusive.","whyNl":"Eisen bepalen wijst op customer, budget autoriseren op sponsor en gebruiken op user. De rollen zijn geen exclusieve functietitels. Eén persoon kan alle drie uitvoeren en de provider wordt daardoor niet de gebruiker namens de klant.","hook":"Classify the action, not the job title.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-004","criterion":"1.1","lo":1,"tag":"Service and offering","prompt":"A description presents a hosted payroll service to a target group, including access and support actions. What is that formal description?","options":["A service offering","A service","A product","A service relationship"],"why":"The question asks about the description of the proposed services, not the arrangement enabling outcomes, the underlying resource configuration or the cooperation itself.","whyNl":"Een formele beschrijving voor een doelgroep is een service offering. De service helpt outcomes te bereiken. Een product is een configuratie van middelen; een service relationship is de samenwerking tussen provider en consument. Kijk naar wat precies benoemd wordt: de beschrijving.","hook":"Offering describes what is offered.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-005","criterion":"1.1","lo":1,"tag":"Service management","prompt":"Which distinction between a practice and service management is correct?","options":["A practice arranges resources for work or an objective; service management concerns capabilities enabling customer value through services","A practice defines service consumption outcomes; service management authorizes the consumer's budget","A practice is the sequence of value chain activities; service management is one activity in that sequence","A practice describes what a customer can buy; service management is the delivery of that description"],"why":"Practices are resource sets supporting work. Service management is the broader capability for enabling value through services; neither is a consumer role or a sales description.","whyNl":"Een practice bundelt organisatorische middelen om werk te doen of een doel te bereiken. Service management is breder: capaciteiten voor waarde via services. De andere opties verwisselen dit met klantrollen, de waardeketen of een service offering.","hook":"Resources for a purpose versus broader service-management capability.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"v2-11-0069","criterion":"1.1","lo":1,"tag":"Service","why":"The decisive clue matches Service: A way for provider and consumer to co-create value by enabling desired outcomes without the consumer managing particular costs and risks. Output instead refers to a tangible or intangible deliverable produced by an activity. Practice instead refers to a set of organizational resources arranged to perform work or achieve an objective.","whyNl":"Een service helpt klanten resultaten te bereiken, terwijl zij bepaalde specifieke kosten en risico's niet zelf hoeven te beheren. Dat betekent niet dat alle kosten en risico's verdwijnen. De klant houdt eigen taken en verantwoordelijkheden. Vergelijk vooral met Output: Output is de concrete oplevering van werk, ook als die digitaal of niet tastbaar is. Een dashboard opleveren is output; dat managers daardoor sneller beslissen is een outcome. Opleveren bewijst dus nog niet dat het gewenste resultaat is bereikt.","hook":"A service enables outcomes; it is not just a product.","prompt":"Which term matches this definition?\nA way for provider and consumer to co-create value by enabling desired outcomes without the consumer managing particular costs and risks.","options":["Service","Output","Practice","Service offering"],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-11-0070","criterion":"1.1","lo":1,"tag":"Service management","why":"The decisive clue matches Service management: The specialized capabilities an organization uses to enable customer value through services. Service instead refers to a way for provider and consumer to co-create value by enabling desired outcomes without the consumer managing particular costs and risks. Service relationship management instead refers to joint provider and consumer activities that sustain value co-creation using agreed service offerings.","whyNl":"Service management is een geheel van organisatorische capaciteiten. Het is breder dan een servicedesk, een proces of één tool: mensen, kennis, technologie en werkwijzen dragen samen bij aan waarde via diensten. Vergelijk vooral met Service: Een service helpt klanten resultaten te bereiken, terwijl zij bepaalde specifieke kosten en risico's niet zelf hoeven te beheren. Dat betekent niet dat alle kosten en risico's verdwijnen. De klant houdt eigen taken en verantwoordelijkheden.","hook":"Organizational capabilities, not a single tool.","prompt":"Which term matches this definition?\nThe specialized capabilities an organization uses to enable customer value through services.","options":["Service management","Service","Service relationship management","Process"],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-11-0071","criterion":"1.1","lo":1,"tag":"Utility","why":"The decisive clue matches Utility: Functionality that meets a consumer's need by supporting performance or removing a constraint. Warranty instead refers to assurance that a service meets its agreed conditions of use, such as availability, capacity, continuity and security. Output instead refers to a tangible or intangible deliverable produced by an activity.","whyNl":"Utility gaat over wat de service mogelijk maakt: de juiste functionaliteit of het wegnemen van een beperking. Een snelle, stabiele dienst heeft niet automatisch utility als de benodigde functie ontbreekt. Vergelijk vooral met Warranty: Warranty gaat over de zekerheid dat de service volgens afspraken bruikbaar is. Het is niet de commerciële garantieperiode en ook niet de lijst functies. Denk aan voldoende capaciteit, beschikbaarheid, continuïteit en beveiliging.","hook":"Fit for purpose = does it do the right thing?","prompt":"Which term matches this definition?\nFunctionality that meets a consumer's need by supporting performance or removing a constraint.","options":["Utility","Warranty","Output","Outcome"],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-11-0072","criterion":"1.1","lo":1,"tag":"Warranty","why":"The decisive clue matches Warranty: Assurance that a service meets its agreed conditions of use, such as availability, capacity, continuity and security. Utility instead refers to functionality that meets a consumer's need by supporting performance or removing a constraint. Value instead refers to the benefits, usefulness and importance perceived by stakeholders.","whyNl":"Warranty gaat over de zekerheid dat de service volgens afspraken bruikbaar is. Het is niet de commerciële garantieperiode en ook niet de lijst functies. Denk aan voldoende capaciteit, beschikbaarheid, continuïteit en beveiliging. Vergelijk vooral met Utility: Utility gaat over wat de service mogelijk maakt: de juiste functionaliteit of het wegnemen van een beperking. Een snelle, stabiele dienst heeft niet automatisch utility als de benodigde functie ontbreekt.","hook":"Fit for use = can it be relied on as agreed?","prompt":"Which term matches this definition?\nAssurance that a service meets its agreed conditions of use, such as availability, capacity, continuity and security.","options":["Warranty","Utility","Value","Output"],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-11-0073","criterion":"1.1","lo":1,"tag":"Customer","why":"The decisive clue matches Customer: The consumer role that sets service requirements and takes responsibility for consumption outcomes. Sponsor instead refers to the consumer role with authority to approve the budget for consuming a service. User instead refers to the role of a person who actually uses a service.","whyNl":"De customer bepaalt wat nodig is en is verantwoordelijk voor de outcomes van het servicegebruik. De sponsor geeft budgetvrijgave; de user gebruikt de service. Eén persoon kan meerdere rollen vervullen: kijk naar de handeling, niet de functietitel. Vergelijk vooral met Sponsor: De sponsor autoriseert het budget. Die rol hoeft de service niet dagelijks te gebruiken of alle eisen op te stellen. Een manager is dus niet automatisch de customer: budgetvrijgave wijst specifiek op sponsor.","hook":"Customer = requirements and outcomes.","prompt":"Which term matches this definition?\nThe consumer role that sets service requirements and takes responsibility for consumption outcomes.","options":["Customer","Sponsor","User","Service provider"],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-11-0074","criterion":"1.1","lo":1,"tag":"User","why":"The decisive clue matches User: The role of a person who actually uses a service. Customer instead refers to the consumer role that sets service requirements and takes responsibility for consumption outcomes. Sponsor instead refers to the consumer role with authority to approve the budget for consuming a service.","whyNl":"User gaat om het daadwerkelijk gebruiken van een dienst. Iemand kan ook klant of sponsor zijn, maar in deze vraag bepaalt het gebruik de rol. Betalen of eisen vaststellen is geen voorwaarde om user te zijn. Vergelijk vooral met Customer: De customer bepaalt wat nodig is en is verantwoordelijk voor de outcomes van het servicegebruik. De sponsor geeft budgetvrijgave; de user gebruikt de service. Eén persoon kan meerdere rollen vervullen: kijk naar de handeling, niet de functietitel.","hook":"User = uses the service.","prompt":"Which term matches this definition?\nThe role of a person who actually uses a service.","options":["User","Customer","Sponsor","Service provider"],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-11-0075","criterion":"1.1","lo":1,"tag":"Sponsor","why":"The decisive clue matches Sponsor: The consumer role with authority to approve the budget for consuming a service. Customer instead refers to the consumer role that sets service requirements and takes responsibility for consumption outcomes. User instead refers to the role of a person who actually uses a service.","whyNl":"De sponsor autoriseert het budget. Die rol hoeft de service niet dagelijks te gebruiken of alle eisen op te stellen. Een manager is dus niet automatisch de customer: budgetvrijgave wijst specifiek op sponsor. Vergelijk vooral met Customer: De customer bepaalt wat nodig is en is verantwoordelijk voor de outcomes van het servicegebruik. De sponsor geeft budgetvrijgave; de user gebruikt de service. Eén persoon kan meerdere rollen vervullen: kijk naar de handeling, niet de functietitel.","hook":"Sponsor = authorizes the budget.","prompt":"Which term matches this definition?\nThe consumer role with authority to approve the budget for consuming a service.","options":["Sponsor","Customer","User","Service provider"],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-11-0076","criterion":"1.1","lo":1,"tag":"Service","why":"The decisive clue matches Service: A way for provider and consumer to co-create value by enabling desired outcomes without the consumer managing particular costs and risks. Output instead refers to a tangible or intangible deliverable produced by an activity. Practice instead refers to a set of organizational resources arranged to perform work or achieve an objective.","whyNl":"Een service helpt klanten resultaten te bereiken, terwijl zij bepaalde specifieke kosten en risico's niet zelf hoeven te beheren. Dat betekent niet dat alle kosten en risico's verdwijnen. De klant houdt eigen taken en verantwoordelijkheden. Vergelijk vooral met Output: Output is de concrete oplevering van werk, ook als die digitaal of niet tastbaar is. Een dashboard opleveren is output; dat managers daardoor sneller beslissen is een outcome. Opleveren bewijst dus nog niet dat het gewenste resultaat is bereikt.","hook":"A service enables outcomes; it is not just a product.","prompt":"Which statement about Service is CORRECT?","options":["A way for provider and consumer to co-create value by enabling desired outcomes without the consumer managing particular costs and risks.","A tangible or intangible deliverable produced by an activity.","A set of organizational resources arranged to perform work or achieve an objective.","A formal description of one or more services aimed at the needs of a particular consumer group."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-11-0077","criterion":"1.1","lo":1,"tag":"Service management","why":"The decisive clue matches Service management: The specialized capabilities an organization uses to enable customer value through services. Service instead refers to a way for provider and consumer to co-create value by enabling desired outcomes without the consumer managing particular costs and risks. Service relationship management instead refers to joint provider and consumer activities that sustain value co-creation using agreed service offerings.","whyNl":"Service management is een geheel van organisatorische capaciteiten. Het is breder dan een servicedesk, een proces of één tool: mensen, kennis, technologie en werkwijzen dragen samen bij aan waarde via diensten. Vergelijk vooral met Service: Een service helpt klanten resultaten te bereiken, terwijl zij bepaalde specifieke kosten en risico's niet zelf hoeven te beheren. Dat betekent niet dat alle kosten en risico's verdwijnen. De klant houdt eigen taken en verantwoordelijkheden.","hook":"Organizational capabilities, not a single tool.","prompt":"Which statement about Service management is CORRECT?","options":["The specialized capabilities an organization uses to enable customer value through services.","A way for provider and consumer to co-create value by enabling desired outcomes without the consumer managing particular costs and risks.","Joint provider and consumer activities that sustain value co-creation using agreed service offerings.","Related activities that turn defined inputs into defined outputs."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-11-0078","criterion":"1.1","lo":1,"tag":"Utility","why":"The decisive clue matches Utility: Functionality that meets a consumer's need by supporting performance or removing a constraint. Warranty instead refers to assurance that a service meets its agreed conditions of use, such as availability, capacity, continuity and security. Output instead refers to a tangible or intangible deliverable produced by an activity.","whyNl":"Utility gaat over wat de service mogelijk maakt: de juiste functionaliteit of het wegnemen van een beperking. Een snelle, stabiele dienst heeft niet automatisch utility als de benodigde functie ontbreekt. Vergelijk vooral met Warranty: Warranty gaat over de zekerheid dat de service volgens afspraken bruikbaar is. Het is niet de commerciële garantieperiode en ook niet de lijst functies. Denk aan voldoende capaciteit, beschikbaarheid, continuïteit en beveiliging.","hook":"Fit for purpose = does it do the right thing?","prompt":"Which statement about Utility is CORRECT?","options":["Functionality that meets a consumer's need by supporting performance or removing a constraint.","Assurance that a service meets its agreed conditions of use, such as availability, capacity, continuity and security.","A tangible or intangible deliverable produced by an activity.","A result achieved for a stakeholder with the help of one or more deliverables."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-11-0079","criterion":"1.1","lo":1,"tag":"Warranty","why":"The decisive clue matches Warranty: Assurance that a service meets its agreed conditions of use, such as availability, capacity, continuity and security. Utility instead refers to functionality that meets a consumer's need by supporting performance or removing a constraint. Value instead refers to the benefits, usefulness and importance perceived by stakeholders.","whyNl":"Warranty gaat over de zekerheid dat de service volgens afspraken bruikbaar is. Het is niet de commerciële garantieperiode en ook niet de lijst functies. Denk aan voldoende capaciteit, beschikbaarheid, continuïteit en beveiliging. Vergelijk vooral met Utility: Utility gaat over wat de service mogelijk maakt: de juiste functionaliteit of het wegnemen van een beperking. Een snelle, stabiele dienst heeft niet automatisch utility als de benodigde functie ontbreekt.","hook":"Fit for use = can it be relied on as agreed?","prompt":"Which statement about Warranty is CORRECT?","options":["Assurance that a service meets its agreed conditions of use, such as availability, capacity, continuity and security.","Functionality that meets a consumer's need by supporting performance or removing a constraint.","The benefits, usefulness and importance perceived by stakeholders.","A tangible or intangible deliverable produced by an activity."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"x101","criterion":"1.1","lo":1,"tag":"Customer and sponsor","prompt":"Which role defines service requirements and is accountable for the outcomes of consuming the service?","options":["Customer","Sponsor","User","Service provider"],"why":"The customer defines requirements and takes responsibility for consumption outcomes. The sponsor authorizes the budget; the user uses the service. One person may hold several roles.","hook":"Requirements and outcomes: customer. Budget: sponsor.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Customer bepaalt eisen en draagt verantwoordelijkheid voor outcomes. Sponsor autoriseert het budget; user gebruikt de service. De provider levert. Kijk naar de beschreven verantwoordelijkheid, niet naar de senioriteit of functietitel. Eén persoon kan meerdere rollen combineren.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x102","criterion":"1.1","lo":1,"tag":"Service management","prompt":"Which description defines service management?","options":["Specialized organizational capabilities for enabling customer value through services","Joint activities by a provider and consumer to maintain their service relationship","A set of connected activities used to deliver a product or service to a consumer","An organization's resources designed to perform work or achieve an objective"],"why":"Service management concerns specialized capabilities for enabling value through services. The other descriptions point toward relationship management, a value stream and a practice.","hook":"Service management: capabilities that enable value.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Service management betreft gespecialiseerde capaciteiten voor klantwaarde via services. Gezamenlijke provider-consumentactiviteiten beschrijven relatiebeheer. Een verbonden werkstroom is iets anders; een set middelen voor een doel is een practice. De brede organisatorische capaciteit is hier bepalend.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x103","criterion":"1.1","lo":1,"tag":"Utility and warranty","prompt":"Complete the statement: [?] describes assurance that a product or service will meet agreed requirements.","options":["Warranty","Utility","Value","Outcome"],"why":"Warranty is assurance that agreed requirements will be met, such as availability, capacity, continuity and security. Utility concerns the functionality offered.","hook":"Warranty: can I rely on it?","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Warranty is de zekerheid dat afgesproken eisen aan gebruik worden gehaald, bijvoorbeeld beschikbaarheid en capaciteit. Utility is benodigde functionaliteit. Value is ervaren nut; outcome is het bereikte stakeholderresultaat. Alleen de aanwezigheid van functies bewijst geen betrouwbare bruikbaarheid.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"missing-word"},{"id":"x104","criterion":"1.1","lo":1,"tag":"Service","prompt":"Which description best defines a service?","options":["A means of enabling joint value creation by helping customers achieve outcomes without managing specific costs and risks","A combination of organizational resources designed to provide value to a consumer","A description of one or more services addressing a target consumer group's needs","A tangible or intangible deliverable produced by carrying out an activity"],"why":"A service helps customers achieve outcomes while the provider takes on specific costs and risks. The alternatives describe a product, a service offering and an output.","hook":"Service: desired outcomes with specific burdens handled for you.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Een service helpt klanten outcomes te bereiken zonder bepaalde specifieke kosten en risico's zelf te beheren. Dat betekent niet dat alle klantverantwoordelijkheid verdwijnt. Middelen configureren beschrijft een product, de formele propositie een offering en een oplevering een output.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-006","criterion":"1.2","lo":1,"tag":"Outputs and outcomes","prompt":"A team delivers an accurate stock report on time, but managers do not use it and shortages remain unchanged. What has been demonstrated?","options":["An output has been delivered; the desired outcome has not been demonstrated","The desired outcome has been delivered because the report is accurate","No output has been delivered because shortages remain unchanged","The output and outcome are the same because both belong to one service"],"why":"The report is a deliverable, whether or not it produces the intended result. Fewer shortages would be a stakeholder result enabled by using it.","whyNl":"Het rapport is output, ook als niemand er iets mee doet. Minder tekorten zou de gewenste outcome zijn. Op tijd en nauwkeurig opleveren bewijst niet dat dat resultaat is bereikt; het uitblijven van resultaat wist de oplevering niet uit.","hook":"Delivery is not proof of the desired result.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-007","criterion":"1.2","lo":1,"tag":"Costs and risks","prompt":"A managed service removes server-maintenance work, but the consumer must train staff and manage supplier dependency. Which value assessment is appropriate?","options":["Consider both costs and risks removed and those introduced by consumption","Compare the service fee with server cost and omit remaining consumer work","Assess introduced risks separately from whether the service offers value","Assume the provider now owns responsibility for the consumer's business outcomes"],"why":"A value assessment includes benefits, costs and risks on both sides of the change. Removing server work does not remove every consumer responsibility.","whyNl":"Beoordeel wat verdwijnt én wat erbij komt. Training kost geld of middelen en leveranciersafhankelijkheid kan risico introduceren. Alleen de factuur met serverkosten vergelijken is te beperkt. De customer blijft verantwoordelijk voor outcomes van het servicegebruik.","hook":"Removed and introduced both matter.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-008","criterion":"1.2","lo":1,"tag":"Value co-creation","prompt":"A provider meets the technical specification, but customers explain that a different result matters to them. What best supports value co-creation?","options":["Work with the customers to understand the needed outcomes and adapt the service relationship","Treat the agreed technical output as sufficient evidence of equal value for every customer","Transfer responsibility for discovering needs entirely to customers after delivery","Use the provider's delivery cost as the measure of customer value"],"why":"Value is co-created through cooperation and depends on what stakeholders need and perceive, not merely on delivered specifications or provider cost.","whyNl":"Technisch opleveren is niet hetzelfde als waarde voor een klant. Provider en consument moeten samen de relevante outcomes begrijpen. De kostprijs van de provider bepaalt geen klantwaarde en verantwoordelijkheid volledig bij de klant leggen is geen gezamenlijke waardecreatie.","hook":"Co-create value rather than declare it delivered.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-009","criterion":"1.2","lo":1,"tag":"Utility and warranty","prompt":"Which TWO statements are correct?\n1. A function can meet a need while its availability remains inadequate.\n2. Meeting availability targets proves the service has the required functions.\n3. Both functionality and agreed conditions of use matter when assessing value.\n4. Utility and warranty are alternative names for the same property.","options":["1 and 3","1 and 2","2 and 4","3 and 4"],"why":"A service can have useful functions but inadequate assurance. Functionality and dependable use are distinct and both contribute to value.","whyNl":"1 is juist: een functie kan nuttig zijn maar te vaak onbeschikbaar. 3 is juist: beide aspecten tellen. 2 verwisselt beschikbaarheid met functionaliteit; 4 maakt twee verschillende begrippen ten onrechte gelijk.","hook":"Useful is not automatically dependable.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"list"},{"id":"v2-12-0080","criterion":"1.2","lo":1,"tag":"Output","why":"The decisive clue matches Output: A tangible or intangible deliverable produced by an activity. Outcome instead refers to a result achieved for a stakeholder with the help of one or more deliverables. Value instead refers to the benefits, usefulness and importance perceived by stakeholders.","whyNl":"Output is de concrete oplevering van werk, ook als die digitaal of niet tastbaar is. Een dashboard opleveren is output; dat managers daardoor sneller beslissen is een outcome. Opleveren bewijst dus nog niet dat het gewenste resultaat is bereikt. Vergelijk vooral met Outcome: Outcome is het resultaat voor de belanghebbende dat door outputs mogelijk wordt. Het is niet het rapport, de code of de installatie zelf. Voorbeeld: minder fouten bij betalingen dankzij een nieuw controlesysteem.","hook":"Output = deliverable.","prompt":"A team delivers a new dashboard. Whether managers make better decisions has not yet been measured.\nWhich option fits this situation?","options":["Output","Outcome","Value","Utility"],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-12-0081","criterion":"1.2","lo":1,"tag":"Outcome","why":"The decisive clue matches Outcome: A result achieved for a stakeholder with the help of one or more deliverables. Output instead refers to a tangible or intangible deliverable produced by an activity. Cost instead refers to money spent on a particular activity or resource.","whyNl":"Outcome is het resultaat voor de belanghebbende dat door outputs mogelijk wordt. Het is niet het rapport, de code of de installatie zelf. Voorbeeld: minder fouten bij betalingen dankzij een nieuw controlesysteem. Vergelijk vooral met Output: Output is de concrete oplevering van werk, ook als die digitaal of niet tastbaar is. Een dashboard opleveren is output; dat managers daardoor sneller beslissen is een outcome. Opleveren bewijst dus nog niet dat het gewenste resultaat is bereikt.","hook":"Outcome = the result for someone.","prompt":"After using a new dashboard, dispatchers reduce missed deliveries.\nWhich option fits this situation?","options":["Outcome","Output","Cost","Warranty"],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-12-0082","criterion":"1.2","lo":1,"tag":"Value","why":"The decisive clue matches Value: The benefits, usefulness and importance perceived by stakeholders. Output instead refers to a tangible or intangible deliverable produced by an activity. Cost instead refers to money spent on a particular activity or resource.","whyNl":"Waarde wordt ervaren door een stakeholder en hangt dus af van diens behoeften. Dezelfde functionaliteit kan voor twee klanten een andere waarde hebben. Alleen prijs, aantal features of gemaakte uren bepaalt waarde niet. Vergelijk vooral met Output: Output is de concrete oplevering van werk, ook als die digitaal of niet tastbaar is. Een dashboard opleveren is output; dat managers daardoor sneller beslissen is een outcome. Opleveren bewijst dus nog niet dat het gewenste resultaat is bereikt.","hook":"Value is perceived, not declared.","prompt":"A customer finds a simple service highly useful, while another customer with different needs does not.\nWhich option fits this situation?","options":["Value","Output","Cost","Warranty"],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-12-0083","criterion":"1.2","lo":1,"tag":"Cost","why":"The decisive clue matches Cost: Money spent on a particular activity or resource. Risk instead refers to uncertainty that can affect objectives, including possible harm, loss or failure to achieve a desired result. Outcome instead refers to a result achieved for a stakeholder with the help of one or more deliverables.","whyNl":"Cost is het geld dat aan werk of middelen wordt besteed. Een service kan kosten wegnemen, zoals eigen serverbeheer, en tegelijk nieuwe kosten opleggen, zoals abonnementen en training. Kijk naar beide kanten. Vergelijk vooral met Risk: Risico gaat over mogelijke gevolgen voor doelen door onzekerheid. Een afhankelijkheid van een leverancier kan een nieuw risico zijn, ook als er nog geen storing is. Een al opgetreden serviceverstoring is een incident; dat is niet hetzelfde als de kans erop.","hook":"Cost = money spent; some costs are removed, others added.","prompt":"Moving to a managed database removes hardware spending but introduces monthly fees.\nWhich option fits this situation?","options":["Cost","Risk","Outcome","Utility"],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-12-0084","criterion":"1.2","lo":1,"tag":"Risk","why":"The decisive clue matches Risk: Uncertainty that can affect objectives, including possible harm, loss or failure to achieve a desired result. Cost instead refers to money spent on a particular activity or resource. Output instead refers to a tangible or intangible deliverable produced by an activity.","whyNl":"Risico gaat over mogelijke gevolgen voor doelen door onzekerheid. Een afhankelijkheid van een leverancier kan een nieuw risico zijn, ook als er nog geen storing is. Een al opgetreden serviceverstoring is een incident; dat is niet hetzelfde als de kans erop. Vergelijk vooral met Cost: Cost is het geld dat aan werk of middelen wordt besteed. Een service kan kosten wegnemen, zoals eigen serverbeheer, en tegelijk nieuwe kosten opleggen, zoals abonnementen en training. Kijk naar beide kanten.","hook":"Risk = uncertainty about effects on objectives.","prompt":"A retailer worries that dependence on one cloud supplier could prevent it from trading during a future outage.\nWhich option fits this situation?","options":["Risk","Cost","Output","Incident"],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-12-0085","criterion":"1.2","lo":1,"tag":"Utility","why":"The decisive clue matches Utility: Functionality that meets a consumer's need by supporting performance or removing a constraint. Output instead refers to a tangible or intangible deliverable produced by an activity. Outcome instead refers to a result achieved for a stakeholder with the help of one or more deliverables.","whyNl":"Utility gaat over wat de service mogelijk maakt: de juiste functionaliteit of het wegnemen van een beperking. Een snelle, stabiele dienst heeft niet automatisch utility als de benodigde functie ontbreekt. Vergelijk vooral met Output: Output is de concrete oplevering van werk, ook als die digitaal of niet tastbaar is. Een dashboard opleveren is output; dat managers daardoor sneller beslissen is een outcome. Opleveren bewijst dus nog niet dat het gewenste resultaat is bereikt.","hook":"Fit for purpose = does it do the right thing?","prompt":"A delivery company needs route planning. Its new app can calculate usable routes, removing the need to plan them manually.\nWhich option fits this situation?","options":["Utility","Output","Outcome","Warranty"],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-12-0086","criterion":"1.2","lo":1,"tag":"Warranty","why":"The decisive clue matches Warranty: Assurance that a service meets its agreed conditions of use, such as availability, capacity, continuity and security. Value instead refers to the benefits, usefulness and importance perceived by stakeholders. Output instead refers to a tangible or intangible deliverable produced by an activity.","whyNl":"Warranty gaat over de zekerheid dat de service volgens afspraken bruikbaar is. Het is niet de commerciële garantieperiode en ook niet de lijst functies. Denk aan voldoende capaciteit, beschikbaarheid, continuïteit en beveiliging. Vergelijk vooral met Value: Waarde wordt ervaren door een stakeholder en hangt dus af van diens behoeften. Dezelfde functionaliteit kan voor twee klanten een andere waarde hebben. Alleen prijs, aantal features of gemaakte uren bepaalt waarde niet.","hook":"Fit for use = can it be relied on as agreed?","prompt":"A route-planning app already has the required functions. The provider now demonstrates that it meets agreed availability and capacity targets.\nWhich option fits this situation?","options":["Warranty","Value","Output","Utility"],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-12-0087","criterion":"1.2","lo":1,"tag":"Output","why":"The decisive clue matches Output: A tangible or intangible deliverable produced by an activity. Outcome instead refers to a result achieved for a stakeholder with the help of one or more deliverables. Value instead refers to the benefits, usefulness and importance perceived by stakeholders.","whyNl":"Output is de concrete oplevering van werk, ook als die digitaal of niet tastbaar is. Een dashboard opleveren is output; dat managers daardoor sneller beslissen is een outcome. Opleveren bewijst dus nog niet dat het gewenste resultaat is bereikt. Vergelijk vooral met Outcome: Outcome is het resultaat voor de belanghebbende dat door outputs mogelijk wordt. Het is niet het rapport, de code of de installatie zelf. Voorbeeld: minder fouten bij betalingen dankzij een nieuw controlesysteem.","hook":"Output = deliverable.","prompt":"Which statement about Output is CORRECT?","options":["A tangible or intangible deliverable produced by an activity.","A result achieved for a stakeholder with the help of one or more deliverables.","The benefits, usefulness and importance perceived by stakeholders.","Functionality that meets a consumer's need by supporting performance or removing a constraint."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-12-0088","criterion":"1.2","lo":1,"tag":"Outcome","why":"The decisive clue matches Outcome: A result achieved for a stakeholder with the help of one or more deliverables. Output instead refers to a tangible or intangible deliverable produced by an activity. Cost instead refers to money spent on a particular activity or resource.","whyNl":"Outcome is het resultaat voor de belanghebbende dat door outputs mogelijk wordt. Het is niet het rapport, de code of de installatie zelf. Voorbeeld: minder fouten bij betalingen dankzij een nieuw controlesysteem. Vergelijk vooral met Output: Output is de concrete oplevering van werk, ook als die digitaal of niet tastbaar is. Een dashboard opleveren is output; dat managers daardoor sneller beslissen is een outcome. Opleveren bewijst dus nog niet dat het gewenste resultaat is bereikt.","hook":"Outcome = the result for someone.","prompt":"Which statement about Outcome is CORRECT?","options":["A result achieved for a stakeholder with the help of one or more deliverables.","A tangible or intangible deliverable produced by an activity.","Money spent on a particular activity or resource.","Assurance that a service meets its agreed conditions of use, such as availability, capacity, continuity and security."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-12-0089","criterion":"1.2","lo":1,"tag":"Value","why":"The decisive clue matches Value: The benefits, usefulness and importance perceived by stakeholders. Output instead refers to a tangible or intangible deliverable produced by an activity. Cost instead refers to money spent on a particular activity or resource.","whyNl":"Waarde wordt ervaren door een stakeholder en hangt dus af van diens behoeften. Dezelfde functionaliteit kan voor twee klanten een andere waarde hebben. Alleen prijs, aantal features of gemaakte uren bepaalt waarde niet. Vergelijk vooral met Output: Output is de concrete oplevering van werk, ook als die digitaal of niet tastbaar is. Een dashboard opleveren is output; dat managers daardoor sneller beslissen is een outcome. Opleveren bewijst dus nog niet dat het gewenste resultaat is bereikt.","hook":"Value is perceived, not declared.","prompt":"Which statement about Value is CORRECT?","options":["The benefits, usefulness and importance perceived by stakeholders.","A tangible or intangible deliverable produced by an activity.","Money spent on a particular activity or resource.","Assurance that a service meets its agreed conditions of use, such as availability, capacity, continuity and security."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-12-0090","criterion":"1.2","lo":1,"tag":"Cost","why":"The decisive clue matches Cost: Money spent on a particular activity or resource. Risk instead refers to uncertainty that can affect objectives, including possible harm, loss or failure to achieve a desired result. Outcome instead refers to a result achieved for a stakeholder with the help of one or more deliverables.","whyNl":"Cost is het geld dat aan werk of middelen wordt besteed. Een service kan kosten wegnemen, zoals eigen serverbeheer, en tegelijk nieuwe kosten opleggen, zoals abonnementen en training. Kijk naar beide kanten. Vergelijk vooral met Risk: Risico gaat over mogelijke gevolgen voor doelen door onzekerheid. Een afhankelijkheid van een leverancier kan een nieuw risico zijn, ook als er nog geen storing is. Een al opgetreden serviceverstoring is een incident; dat is niet hetzelfde als de kans erop.","hook":"Cost = money spent; some costs are removed, others added.","prompt":"Which statement about Cost is CORRECT?","options":["Money spent on a particular activity or resource.","Uncertainty that can affect objectives, including possible harm, loss or failure to achieve a desired result.","A result achieved for a stakeholder with the help of one or more deliverables.","Functionality that meets a consumer's need by supporting performance or removing a constraint."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-12-0091","criterion":"1.2","lo":1,"tag":"Risk","why":"The decisive clue matches Risk: Uncertainty that can affect objectives, including possible harm, loss or failure to achieve a desired result. Cost instead refers to money spent on a particular activity or resource. Output instead refers to a tangible or intangible deliverable produced by an activity.","whyNl":"Risico gaat over mogelijke gevolgen voor doelen door onzekerheid. Een afhankelijkheid van een leverancier kan een nieuw risico zijn, ook als er nog geen storing is. Een al opgetreden serviceverstoring is een incident; dat is niet hetzelfde als de kans erop. Vergelijk vooral met Cost: Cost is het geld dat aan werk of middelen wordt besteed. Een service kan kosten wegnemen, zoals eigen serverbeheer, en tegelijk nieuwe kosten opleggen, zoals abonnementen en training. Kijk naar beide kanten.","hook":"Risk = uncertainty about effects on objectives.","prompt":"Which statement about Risk is CORRECT?","options":["Uncertainty that can affect objectives, including possible harm, loss or failure to achieve a desired result.","Money spent on a particular activity or resource.","A tangible or intangible deliverable produced by an activity.","An unplanned interruption to a service or an unplanned reduction in its quality."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"x105","criterion":"1.2","lo":1,"tag":"Output and outcome","prompt":"A reporting service produces a daily stock report. Store managers use it to reduce shortages. Which pairing is correct?","options":["Daily report: output; fewer shortages: outcome","Daily report: outcome; fewer shortages: output","Daily report: warranty; fewer shortages: utility","Daily report: utility; fewer shortages: warranty"],"why":"The report is a deliverable, so it is an output. Fewer shortages are a result enabled for stakeholders, so they are an outcome. Producing the report does not guarantee that result.","hook":"Output: what is delivered. Outcome: what changes for someone.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Het dagrapport is wat geleverd wordt: output. Minder tekorten is wat managers daarmee bereiken: outcome. Het rapport kan op tijd zijn geleverd zonder dat tekorten dalen. Utility en warranty onderscheiden functionaliteit en afgesproken bruikbaarheid, niet oplevering en effect.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x106","criterion":"1.2","lo":1,"tag":"Utility and warranty","prompt":"A booking service has every required booking function but becomes unavailable during agreed opening hours. Which assessment is best supported?","options":["Its utility is supported, but its warranty is not being met","Its warranty is supported, but its utility is not being met","Its utility and warranty are both demonstrated by the available functions","Its utility is absent because availability is a functional requirement"],"why":"The functionality supports utility. Failure to meet agreed availability undermines warranty. A useful function and dependable delivery are separate considerations.","hook":"Right functions, unreliable delivery: utility without adequate warranty.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"De functies ondersteunen de behoefte: utility. Uitval tijdens afgesproken openingstijden schendt warranty. Beschikbaarheid is geen bewijs van de juiste functie en ontbrekende beschikbaarheid betekent niet automatisch dat de functie zelf ontbreekt. Beide aspecten moet je apart beoordelen.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x107","criterion":"1.2","lo":1,"tag":"Costs and risks","prompt":"A hosted payroll service removes the need to maintain servers. The customer now pays subscription fees and depends on an external provider. What does this illustrate?","options":["A service can remove some consumer costs and risks while introducing others","A service transfers the customer's accountability for business outcomes to the provider","A service removes costs, while introduced risks are outside the value assessment","A service creates value whenever its fee is lower than the cost of the servers"],"why":"Consumers consider costs and risks removed as well as those introduced. Server savings alone do not establish value, and the customer remains responsible for the outcomes of consumption.","hook":"Check both sides: burdens removed and burdens added.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Serverbeheer kan verdwijnen terwijl abonnementen, training en leveranciersafhankelijkheid erbij komen. Beoordeel kosten en risico's die verdwijnen én ontstaan. De serverbesparing alleen bewijst geen waarde. De customer houdt verantwoordelijkheid voor de outcomes van het gebruik.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x108","criterion":"1.2","lo":1,"tag":"Value","prompt":"Two customers receive the same reports at the same price. One makes faster decisions; the other finds the reports irrelevant. Which explanation best fits ITIL?","options":["Value depends on stakeholder perceptions and the outcomes important to them","Value is the same because both customers receive identical outputs","Value is fixed by the provider when it sets the price of the service","Value is determined by report availability rather than customer use"],"why":"Value depends on perceived benefits, usefulness and importance. Identical outputs or prices can have different value in different stakeholder contexts.","hook":"Same output can mean different value.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Waarde hangt af van behoeften en ervaren nut voor stakeholders. Dezelfde output en prijs kunnen daarom verschillende waarde hebben. De provider bepaalt niet eenzijdig de ervaren waarde. Beschikbaarheid helpt, maar bewijst niet dat de klant er iets belangrijks mee bereikt.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-010","criterion":"1.3","lo":1,"tag":"Service offering","prompt":"A provider retains ownership of a server but lets a customer use its computing capacity. Which offering component is this?","options":["Access to resources","Goods","Service actions","Transfer of service ownership"],"why":"Access lets the consumer use a resource while the provider retains ownership. Goods involve ownership transfer; service actions are performed activities.","whyNl":"De klant gebruikt capaciteit zonder eigenaar te worden: access to resources. Goods vereist eigendomsoverdracht. Service actions betreft uitgevoerd werk. De toegang draagt niet automatisch eigendom van de service over.","hook":"Use without ownership transfer.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-011","criterion":"1.3","lo":1,"tag":"Service relationship activities","prompt":"The provider maintains its platform. The consumer trains its own users. Together they review cooperation. Which order correctly identifies these activities?","options":["Service provision; service consumption; service relationship management","Service consumption; service provision; service relationship management","Service provision; service relationship management; service consumption","Service relationship management; service consumption; service provision"],"why":"Provider-side delivery, consumer-side use and joint management of the relationship are distinct but connected activities.","whyNl":"Het platform onderhouden is providerwerk: provision. Eigen gebruikers voorbereiden is consumentwerk: consumption. Samen de samenwerking beheren is relationship management. Niet elke activiteit waarbij een provider betrokken is, is automatisch gezamenlijk relatiebeheer.","hook":"Provider work; consumer work; joint relationship work.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-012","criterion":"1.3","lo":1,"tag":"Consumer responsibilities","prompt":"A customer buys a managed collaboration service. Which activity is still an example of service consumption?","options":["Managing the customer's own resources needed to use the service","Operating the provider's platform as part of the agreed hosting service","Publishing the provider's formal description of the offering","Managing the provider's resources required to supply the service"],"why":"Consumption includes the consumer's resources and actions required for use. The other activities are on the provider or offering side of the relationship.","whyNl":"De consument houdt eigen activiteiten, zoals medewerkers en gebruiksrechten beheren. Het platform en providermiddelen exploiteren zijn provision. Een formele propositie publiceren gaat over de offering. Managed betekent dus niet dat de klant niets meer hoeft te doen.","hook":"Consumption still includes the consumer's work.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"v2-13-0092","criterion":"1.3","lo":1,"tag":"Service provider","why":"The decisive clue matches Service provider: An organization acting in the role of delivering services to a consumer. Customer instead refers to the consumer role that sets service requirements and takes responsibility for consumption outcomes. User instead refers to the role of a person who actually uses a service.","whyNl":"Een serviceprovider levert de dienst. Dat kan een externe onderneming zijn, maar ook een interne IT-afdeling. Een organisatie kan tegelijk provider van de ene dienst en consument van een andere dienst zijn. Vergelijk vooral met Customer: De customer bepaalt wat nodig is en is verantwoordelijk voor de outcomes van het servicegebruik. De sponsor geeft budgetvrijgave; de user gebruikt de service. Eén persoon kan meerdere rollen vervullen: kijk naar de handeling, niet de functietitel.","hook":"Provider = supplies the service.","prompt":"An internal IT department operates a file-sharing service for other departments. In that relationship, what role does the IT department have\nWhich option fits this situation?","options":["Service provider","Customer","User","Sponsor"],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-13-0093","criterion":"1.3","lo":1,"tag":"Service offering","why":"The decisive clue matches Service offering: A formal description of one or more services aimed at the needs of a particular consumer group. Service relationship management instead refers to joint provider and consumer activities that sustain value co-creation using agreed service offerings. Service instead refers to a way for provider and consumer to co-create value by enabling desired outcomes without the consumer managing particular costs and risks.","whyNl":"Een service offering beschrijft het aanbod voor een doelgroep. Het kan goederen, toegang tot resources en service actions bevatten. Een service offering is niet uitsluitend een prijs of een SLA; het maakt duidelijk wat de consument krijgt. Vergelijk vooral met Service relationship management: Dit gaat om gezamenlijke activiteiten van provider en consument, zoals overleggen over behoeften en resultaten. Dat is specifieker dan alle leverancierstaken of alle gebruikerstaken. Let op het woord samen.","hook":"Offering = the described package for a target group.","prompt":"A provider describes a starter package for small charities, combining hosted accounts, a supplied device and onboarding support.\nWhich option fits this situation?","options":["Service offering","Service relationship management","Service","Output"],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-13-0094","criterion":"1.3","lo":1,"tag":"Service provision","why":"The decisive clue matches Service provision: Activities the provider performs to supply services, manage its resources and fulfil agreed service actions. Service consumption instead refers to activities the consumer performs to use services, including managing its own resources and carrying out user actions. Service relationship management instead refers to joint provider and consumer activities that sustain value co-creation using agreed service offerings.","whyNl":"Service provision is de leverende kant van de relatie: de provider beheert eigen middelen en voert afgesproken service actions uit. De consument heeft daarnaast eigen activiteiten; ITIL verdeelt niet alle verantwoordelijkheid naar de provider. Vergelijk vooral met Service consumption: Service consumption is de consumentenkant. De klant kan eigen mensen, toegang en benodigde acties moeten organiseren. Een gehoste service maakt de consument niet passief en neemt niet alle verantwoordelijkheden over.","hook":"Provision = provider-side activities.","prompt":"A hosting company maintains its servers and performs agreed backup actions for a customer.\nWhich option fits this situation?","options":["Service provision","Service consumption","Service relationship management","Service offering"],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-13-0095","criterion":"1.3","lo":1,"tag":"Service consumption","why":"The decisive clue matches Service consumption: Activities the consumer performs to use services, including managing its own resources and carrying out user actions. Service provision instead refers to activities the provider performs to supply services, manage its resources and fulfil agreed service actions. Service relationship management instead refers to joint provider and consumer activities that sustain value co-creation using agreed service offerings.","whyNl":"Service consumption is de consumentenkant. De klant kan eigen mensen, toegang en benodigde acties moeten organiseren. Een gehoste service maakt de consument niet passief en neemt niet alle verantwoordelijkheden over. Vergelijk vooral met Service provision: Service provision is de leverende kant van de relatie: de provider beheert eigen middelen en voert afgesproken service actions uit. De consument heeft daarnaast eigen activiteiten; ITIL verdeelt niet alle verantwoordelijkheid naar de provider.","hook":"Consumption = consumer-side activities.","prompt":"A customer trains its staff and manages the devices those staff use to access a hosted service.\nWhich option fits this situation?","options":["Service consumption","Service provision","Service relationship management","Service offering"],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-13-0096","criterion":"1.3","lo":1,"tag":"Service relationship management","why":"The decisive clue matches Service relationship management: Joint provider and consumer activities that sustain value co-creation using agreed service offerings. Service provision instead refers to activities the provider performs to supply services, manage its resources and fulfil agreed service actions. Service consumption instead refers to activities the consumer performs to use services, including managing its own resources and carrying out user actions.","whyNl":"Dit gaat om gezamenlijke activiteiten van provider en consument, zoals overleggen over behoeften en resultaten. Dat is specifieker dan alle leverancierstaken of alle gebruikerstaken. Let op het woord samen. Vergelijk vooral met Service provision: Service provision is de leverende kant van de relatie: de provider beheert eigen middelen en voert afgesproken service actions uit. De consument heeft daarnaast eigen activiteiten; ITIL verdeelt niet alle verantwoordelijkheid naar de provider.","hook":"Relationship management here = provider and consumer together.","prompt":"A provider and its customer regularly review changing needs and agree how their service arrangement should evolve.\nWhich option fits this situation?","options":["Service relationship management","Service provision","Service consumption","Service offering"],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-13-0097","criterion":"1.3","lo":1,"tag":"Service provider","why":"The decisive clue matches Service provider: An organization acting in the role of delivering services to a consumer. Customer instead refers to the consumer role that sets service requirements and takes responsibility for consumption outcomes. User instead refers to the role of a person who actually uses a service.","whyNl":"Een serviceprovider levert de dienst. Dat kan een externe onderneming zijn, maar ook een interne IT-afdeling. Een organisatie kan tegelijk provider van de ene dienst en consument van een andere dienst zijn. Vergelijk vooral met Customer: De customer bepaalt wat nodig is en is verantwoordelijk voor de outcomes van het servicegebruik. De sponsor geeft budgetvrijgave; de user gebruikt de service. Eén persoon kan meerdere rollen vervullen: kijk naar de handeling, niet de functietitel.","hook":"Provider = supplies the service.","prompt":"Which statement about Service provider is CORRECT?","options":["An organization acting in the role of delivering services to a consumer.","The consumer role that sets service requirements and takes responsibility for consumption outcomes.","The role of a person who actually uses a service.","The consumer role with authority to approve the budget for consuming a service."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-13-0098","criterion":"1.3","lo":1,"tag":"Service offering","why":"The decisive clue matches Service offering: A formal description of one or more services aimed at the needs of a particular consumer group. Service relationship management instead refers to joint provider and consumer activities that sustain value co-creation using agreed service offerings. Service instead refers to a way for provider and consumer to co-create value by enabling desired outcomes without the consumer managing particular costs and risks.","whyNl":"Een service offering beschrijft het aanbod voor een doelgroep. Het kan goederen, toegang tot resources en service actions bevatten. Een service offering is niet uitsluitend een prijs of een SLA; het maakt duidelijk wat de consument krijgt. Vergelijk vooral met Service relationship management: Dit gaat om gezamenlijke activiteiten van provider en consument, zoals overleggen over behoeften en resultaten. Dat is specifieker dan alle leverancierstaken of alle gebruikerstaken. Let op het woord samen.","hook":"Offering = the described package for a target group.","prompt":"Which statement about Service offering is CORRECT?","options":["A formal description of one or more services aimed at the needs of a particular consumer group.","Joint provider and consumer activities that sustain value co-creation using agreed service offerings.","A way for provider and consumer to co-create value by enabling desired outcomes without the consumer managing particular costs and risks.","A tangible or intangible deliverable produced by an activity."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-13-0099","criterion":"1.3","lo":1,"tag":"Service provision","why":"The decisive clue matches Service provision: Activities the provider performs to supply services, manage its resources and fulfil agreed service actions. Service consumption instead refers to activities the consumer performs to use services, including managing its own resources and carrying out user actions. Service relationship management instead refers to joint provider and consumer activities that sustain value co-creation using agreed service offerings.","whyNl":"Service provision is de leverende kant van de relatie: de provider beheert eigen middelen en voert afgesproken service actions uit. De consument heeft daarnaast eigen activiteiten; ITIL verdeelt niet alle verantwoordelijkheid naar de provider. Vergelijk vooral met Service consumption: Service consumption is de consumentenkant. De klant kan eigen mensen, toegang en benodigde acties moeten organiseren. Een gehoste service maakt de consument niet passief en neemt niet alle verantwoordelijkheden over.","hook":"Provision = provider-side activities.","prompt":"Which statement about Service provision is CORRECT?","options":["Activities the provider performs to supply services, manage its resources and fulfil agreed service actions.","Activities the consumer performs to use services, including managing its own resources and carrying out user actions.","Joint provider and consumer activities that sustain value co-creation using agreed service offerings.","A formal description of one or more services aimed at the needs of a particular consumer group."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-13-0100","criterion":"1.3","lo":1,"tag":"Service consumption","why":"The decisive clue matches Service consumption: Activities the consumer performs to use services, including managing its own resources and carrying out user actions. Service provision instead refers to activities the provider performs to supply services, manage its resources and fulfil agreed service actions. Service relationship management instead refers to joint provider and consumer activities that sustain value co-creation using agreed service offerings.","whyNl":"Service consumption is de consumentenkant. De klant kan eigen mensen, toegang en benodigde acties moeten organiseren. Een gehoste service maakt de consument niet passief en neemt niet alle verantwoordelijkheden over. Vergelijk vooral met Service provision: Service provision is de leverende kant van de relatie: de provider beheert eigen middelen en voert afgesproken service actions uit. De consument heeft daarnaast eigen activiteiten; ITIL verdeelt niet alle verantwoordelijkheid naar de provider.","hook":"Consumption = consumer-side activities.","prompt":"Which statement about Service consumption is CORRECT?","options":["Activities the consumer performs to use services, including managing its own resources and carrying out user actions.","Activities the provider performs to supply services, manage its resources and fulfil agreed service actions.","Joint provider and consumer activities that sustain value co-creation using agreed service offerings.","A formal description of one or more services aimed at the needs of a particular consumer group."],"kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"x109","criterion":"1.3","lo":1,"tag":"Service consumption","prompt":"A customer manages employee access to an online learning service and gives the provider feedback. Which service relationship concept includes these activities?","options":["Service consumption","Service provision","Service offering","Service relationship management"],"why":"Consumption includes the consumer's management of resources needed to use a service, use of the service and feedback. Provision describes the provider's activities; an offering describes what is offered.","hook":"Consumption includes managing use and giving feedback.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"Dit zijn activiteiten aan de consumentkant: eigen gebruiksmiddelen beheren en feedback leveren hoort bij service consumption. De provider exploiteert de dienst via provision. Een offering beschrijft wat geleverd kan worden; gezamenlijk relatiebeheer benadrukt activiteiten van beide partijen samen.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x110","criterion":"1.3","lo":1,"tag":"Service offering","prompt":"An offering includes a laptop whose ownership passes to the customer, access to a hosted application, and help with installation. Which classification is correct?","options":["Goods, access to resources, and service actions","Resources, service actions, and goods","Service actions, goods, and access to resources","Access to resources, goods, and service actions"],"why":"The transferred laptop is goods. The hosted application provides access without transferring ownership. Installation assistance is a service action.","hook":"Own it, access it, or have something done.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"De laptop wordt eigendom: goods. De applicatie wordt gebruikt zonder eigendomsoverdracht: access to resources. Installatiehulp is verricht werk: service actions. De alternatieven gebruiken dezelfde begrippen maar koppelen ze aan het verkeerde onderdeel.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-013","criterion":"2.1","lo":2,"tag":"Using guiding principles","prompt":"A principle remains useful after an organization changes its strategy. What best explains this?","options":["Guiding principles are recommendations intended to guide many circumstances","Guiding principles apply only while the original strategy remains approved","Each strategy selects one principle and suspends the remaining principles","Principles prescribe the same detailed procedure for every strategy"],"why":"Principles offer broadly applicable guidance, rather than strategy-specific procedures or mutually exclusive rules.","whyNl":"Guiding principles bieden brede aanbevelingen. Een strategiewijziging maakt ze niet automatisch ongeldig. De organisatie kiest niet één principe dat de andere uitschakelt en de principes schrijven ook geen universele detailprocedure voor.","hook":"General guidance, adapted to the circumstances.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-014","criterion":"2.1","lo":2,"tag":"Using guiding principles","prompt":"A team improves a service by considering user value, observing existing work and using feedback. How should its use of principles be understood?","options":["Several principles complement one another in the same situation","Only the first principle used applies to the decision","Each principle must be assigned to a different team","Using several principles turns them into value chain activities"],"why":"Principles interact and support one another. They are not exclusive selections or organizational assignments.","whyNl":"Verschillende principes ondersteunen dezelfde beslissing. Waarde begrijpen, de huidige situatie beoordelen en feedback gebruiken kunnen samen. Dat maakt principes geen fasen, teams of value-chainactiviteiten.","hook":"Consider principles together.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-015","criterion":"2.1","lo":2,"tag":"Using guiding principles","prompt":"Which TWO statements describe guiding principles correctly?\n1. They may help with decisions in any practice.\n2. They specify a compulsory lifecycle order.\n3. Their relevance should be considered together in context.\n4. They replace the need to understand stakeholder needs.","options":["1 and 3","1 and 2","2 and 4","3 and 4"],"why":"Principles are broadly applicable and should be considered as a connected set. They do not replace understanding the situation or impose a lifecycle sequence.","whyNl":"1 en 3 zijn juist. Principes geven richting binnen uiteenlopende practices en werken samen. 2 verwart ze met verplichte fasen; 4 negeert juist het begrijpen van stakeholders, wat essentieel blijft.","hook":"Recommendations, not lifecycle phases.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"list"},{"id":"v2-21-0001","criterion":"2.1","lo":2,"tag":"Using guiding principles","prompt":"Which statement BEST describes how the ITIL guiding principles should be used?","options":["They should be considered together and adapted to the circumstances","Each principle belongs to one specific practice","They form a mandatory sequence that must be followed in order","An organization should select one principle and ignore the others"],"why":"The guiding principles are universal recommendations that interact and should be applied together as relevant to the situation.","whyNl":"Gebruik de principes samen en pas ze toe op de situatie. Het zijn geen fasen, geen één-op-één koppeling aan practices en geen keuze voor slechts één principe.","hook":"Principles interact; they are not a sequence.","kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-21-0002","criterion":"2.1","lo":2,"tag":"Using guiding principles","prompt":"A team is working in unfamiliar circumstances. What is the BEST way to use the guiding principles?","options":["Use all relevant principles as guidance while adapting decisions to the context","Choose the principle that sounds most important and use only that one","Apply them as fixed procedures without considering the situation","Use them only after a service has already been designed"],"why":"The principles guide decisions in many circumstances but do not replace judgement or context.","whyNl":"De principes geven richting in allerlei omstandigheden, maar zijn geen vaste procedures. Context en professioneel oordeel blijven nodig.","hook":"Guidance + context, not rigid rules.","kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-21-0003","criterion":"2.1","lo":2,"tag":"Using guiding principles","prompt":"Which statement about the scope of the guiding principles is CORRECT?","options":["They can guide organizations regardless of changes in goals, strategies or types of work","They apply only to service management improvement initiatives","They apply only to the six service value chain activities","They apply only when an organization adopts every ITIL practice"],"why":"The principles are intended to guide an organization broadly, including when its objectives or circumstances change.","whyNl":"De principes zijn breed toepasbaar en niet beperkt tot één soort initiatief, value-chainactiviteit of volledige ITIL-adoptie.","hook":"Broadly applicable guidance.","kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-21-0004","criterion":"2.1","lo":2,"tag":"Using guiding principles","prompt":"Which is the MOST appropriate relationship between the guiding principles and organizational decisions?","options":["The principles influence decisions without dictating one mandatory action in every case","Each principle defines one compulsory process that must be implemented","The principles replace governance decisions when teams disagree","Only senior management should use the principles"],"why":"Guiding principles inform and shape decisions; they are not rigid process instructions and are relevant across the organization.","whyNl":"Principes sturen het denken, maar schrijven niet voor elke situatie één verplichte actie voor. Ze zijn niet alleen voor management.","hook":"Guide decisions; do not dictate procedures.","kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-21-0005","criterion":"2.1","lo":2,"tag":"Using guiding principles","prompt":"Which TWO statements about the guiding principles are correct?\n1. They are recommendations that can guide an organization in all circumstances.\n2. They are used independently so that one principle does not affect another.\n3. They should be considered together when making decisions.\n4. They prescribe a fixed order for service management work.","options":["1 and 3","1 and 2","2 and 4","3 and 4"],"why":"Statements 1 and 3 are correct. The principles are broadly applicable and interact; they are not independent stages or a fixed sequence.","whyNl":"1 en 3 zijn juist. Principes zijn breed toepasbaar en werken samen; ze zijn geen losse fasen en hebben geen vaste volgorde.","hook":"Broad guidance, used together.","kind":"list","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-21-0006","criterion":"2.1","lo":2,"tag":"Using guiding principles","prompt":"Which statement is NOT consistent with the nature of the guiding principles?","options":["Each principle must be completed before the next principle is considered","Several principles may be relevant to the same decision","The principles can support decisions when circumstances change","The principles are intended as recommendations rather than rigid instructions"],"why":"The principles are not sequential stages. Several can apply at once and they are used as recommendations.","whyNl":"De principes vormen geen stappenplan. Meerdere principes kunnen tegelijk relevant zijn en ze zijn bedoeld als aanbevelingen.","hook":"Not a sequence.","kind":"negative","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"v2-21-0007","criterion":"2.1","lo":2,"tag":"Using guiding principles","prompt":"An organization changes its sourcing strategy and operating model. How should the guiding principles be treated?","options":["Continue using the relevant principles as guidance in the new circumstances","Replace them with a new set because they only apply to the old operating model","Use only 'think and work holistically' because sourcing has changed","Suspend them until all new processes are documented"],"why":"The guiding principles remain applicable when strategies, goals or organizational structures change.","whyNl":"Ook bij een andere sourcingstrategie of organisatiestructuur blijven de relevante principes bruikbaar.","hook":"Principles survive changes in context.","kind":"standard","challenge":true,"pool":"exam-v2","reviewed":true},{"id":"x201","criterion":"2.1","lo":2,"tag":"Using the principles","prompt":"A team uses \"start where you are\" and \"progress iteratively with feedback\" on the same improvement. What explains this?","options":["The principles interact and should be considered together in the situation","Each principle applies to a different mandatory phase of the service lifecycle","One principle must be completed before another becomes applicable","The first principle controls planning and the second is limited to development"],"why":"Guiding principles are broadly applicable and interact. They are not sequential phases or rules assigned to individual practices.","hook":"Principles work together; they are not a sequence.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"De principes zijn geen verplichte fasen en niet exclusief voor één practice of type werk. Eerst de huidige situatie begrijpen en vervolgens iteratief verbeteren kan in dezelfde situatie logisch zijn. Principes vullen elkaar aan; je moet hun gezamenlijke relevantie bekijken.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"x202","criterion":"2.1","lo":2,"tag":"Using the principles","prompt":"Which TWO statements about the guiding principles are correct?\n1. They can guide an organization when its goals or circumstances change.\n2. Each principle belongs to one value chain activity.\n3. They should be considered together rather than in isolation.\n4. An organization must choose one principle to govern all its decisions.","options":["1 and 3","1 and 2","2 and 4","3 and 4"],"why":"The principles remain useful across circumstances and complement each other. They are neither allocated one per activity nor mutually exclusive choices.","hook":"Broad guidance, used together.","challenge":true,"whyNl":"1 en 3 zijn juist: principes blijven bruikbaar bij veranderende omstandigheden en horen samen overwogen te worden. 2 verdeelt ze ten onrechte over exclusieve activiteiten. 4 maakt er een keuze tussen onderling uitsluitende regels van. Het zijn samenhangende aanbevelingen.","pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"list"},{"id":"contrast-016","criterion":"2.2","lo":2,"tag":"Focus on value","prompt":"A team can add a requested feature cheaply, but first asks whether it will help users complete the task that matters to them. Which principle is emphasized?","options":["Focus on value","Keep it simple and practical","Start where you are","Optimize and automate"],"why":"The decision is anchored in the consumer's useful result. Low cost is background, not evidence that the team is simplifying or automating work.","whyNl":"De doorslag geeft wat gebruikers bereiken. Dat de feature goedkoop is, maakt dit geen keep it simple of optimize and automate. De huidige situatie objectief bekijken zou start where you are zijn; hier staat gebruikerswaarde voorop.","hook":"What useful result will this create?","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-017","criterion":"2.2","lo":2,"tag":"Start where you are","prompt":"An existing service has a poor reputation. Before replacing it, the team checks direct observations rather than assuming every part is unusable. Which principle is emphasized?","options":["Start where you are","Focus on value","Think and work holistically","Progress iteratively with feedback"],"why":"The team establishes the actual starting point and what is useful. It has not yet divided implementation into feedback-driven increments.","whyNl":"Het team beoordeelt de werkelijke bestaande situatie. Slechte reputatie bewijst niet dat alles weg moet. Holistisch kijken betreft het gehele systeem; iteratief werken vraagt kleine uitvoeringsstappen met feedback. Die zijn hier nog niet beschreven.","hook":"Assess before discarding.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-018","criterion":"2.2","lo":2,"tag":"Iteration and collaboration","prompt":"All teams share a dashboard, but they plan to wait until the whole programme is complete before reviewing effects. Which principle would most directly improve how the work progresses?","options":["Progress iteratively with feedback","Collaborate and promote visibility","Start where you are","Keep it simple and practical"],"why":"Visibility is already present. What is missing is timely feedback that changes subsequent increments of work.","whyNl":"De gedeelde informatie ondersteunt al visibility. Het probleem is wachten met feedback tot alles af is. Kleine stappen met tijdige feedback verbeteren juist het verloop van het werk. Simpel houden of een nulmeting lost dat gemis niet specifiek op.","hook":"Visible work still needs timely feedback.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-019","criterion":"2.2","lo":2,"tag":"Collaboration and holistic thinking","prompt":"A team already understands the end-to-end service, but relevant specialists cannot access the decisions or contribute their knowledge. Which principle is most directly missing?","options":["Collaborate and promote visibility","Think and work holistically","Optimize and automate","Start where you are"],"why":"The stated gap is participation and information access, not knowledge of the overall system.","whyNl":"Het geheel is al in beeld. Het ontbreekt aan mensen betrekken en informatie zichtbaar maken: collaborate and promote visibility. Holistic thinking is dus niet de beste keuze voor precies dit beschreven tekort.","hook":"Understanding the whole is not the same as involving people.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-020","criterion":"2.2","lo":2,"tag":"Holistic thinking","prompt":"A team proposes a change that improves its response target but transfers extra work to another team and slows the customer journey. Which principle most directly challenges the proposal?","options":["Think and work holistically","Collaborate and promote visibility","Keep it simple and practical","Progress iteratively with feedback"],"why":"The proposal optimizes a part at the expense of the whole. Communication and iteration may help, but the decisive assessment is end-to-end value.","whyNl":"De lokale score verbetert terwijl de hele service slechter wordt. Dat vraagt holistic thinking. Samenwerken en itereren kunnen helpen, maar de kern van de fout is optimaliseren van één deel ten koste van het geheel.","hook":"Optimize the service, not just one team's metric.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"},{"id":"contrast-021","criterion":"2.2","lo":2,"tag":"Simplicity and automation","prompt":"A workflow contains duplicate information entry. The team removes the duplicate step while keeping the needed check. No technology change is involved. Which principle is most directly illustrated?","options":["Keep it simple and practical","Optimize and automate","Collaborate and promote visibility","Progress iteratively with feedback"],"why":"The action removes unnecessary complexity without discarding a useful control. There is no described use of automation.","whyNl":"Onnodig werk wordt weggehaald en noodzakelijke controle blijft. Dat is keep it simple and practical. Verbeteren kan ook bij optimize horen, maar de expliciete nadruk hier is eenvoud zonder een automatiseringsstap.","hook":"Remove waste without removing necessary controls.","challenge":true,"pool":"contrast","reviewed":true,"kind":"standard"}]);
